Good — now let’s take this from “it works locally” → production-grade auto refresh

Right now you manually do:

curl -X POST http://localhost:8099/actuator/refresh

👉 That does NOT scale in microservices.

🚀 Goal (What we’re building)

When you update config in Git:

👉 ALL services refresh automatically
👉 No manual curl
👉 No restarts

In real production, you don’t manually call /refresh:

👉 You use:

Spring Cloud Bus (Kafka/RabbitMQ)
Auto refresh across all instances

🧠 How this works (High-level)

We introduce:

🔹 Spring Cloud Bus
Uses a message broker
Broadcasts config change events

🔹 Message Broker (Kafka or RabbitMQ)
Sends refresh events to all services

